+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI automation tools in 2026?
+For most teams, the strongest starting points are `n8n`, `Activepieces`, `Flowise`, `Langflow`, `AutoGen`, and `CrewAI`. The right choice depends on whether you want visual workflows, code-first orchestration, browser automation, or MCP-based tool execution.
+
+### Which open source AI automation tools are self-hosted?
+Most repositories on this list are self-hostable because they are public GitHub projects. Strong self-hosted options include `n8n`, `Activepieces`, `Flowise`, `Langflow`, `allama`, and `BuildShip`.
+
+### What is the best GitHub-based alternative to proprietary AI workflow SaaS?
+`n8n` and `Activepieces` are the clearest GitHub-based alternatives when you want visual automation. If you want agent graphs rather than classic workflow nodes, `Flowise`, `Langflow`, and `LangGraph` are usually better fits.
+
+### Which open source AI automation tools work with MCP?
+Good MCP-related repos here include `Apify MCP Server`, `mcp-server-excel`, `mcp-server-js`, `Blender MCP Server`, and `codebase-mcp`. They are useful when you want a standard tool interface for agent systems.
+
+### Are there open source AI automation tools for browser and desktop tasks?
+Yes. `RPA Framework`, `AgentQL`, `HEC-Commander`, and `Apify MCP Server` cover browser or operator-style automation. `Blender MCP Server` shows how AI automation can also reach desktop application environments.
+
+### Which open source AI automation repositories are best for developer workflows?
+For engineering-heavy use cases, start with `CodeMachine-CLI`, `aidevops`, `ops0-cli`, `reviewcerberus`, `codescan`, and `codebase-mcp`. These are better aligned with repos, CI, terminal work, and code review than general business automation tools.
