+## TL;DR
+- `n8n`, `Activepieces`, `Flowise`, `Langflow`, and `BuildShip` are the strongest visual workflow builders for AI-first automation.
+- `AutoGen`, `CrewAI`, `AutoGPT`, `LangGraph`, and `Connery SDK` are solid choices when you need multi-agent orchestration and tool calling.
+- `RPA Framework`, `Robot Framework`, `TagUI`, `OpenRPA`, and `AgentQL` are useful when you need browser, desktop, or document automation.
+- `Apify MCP Server`, `mcp-server-excel`, `mcp-server-js`, and `Blender MCP Server` are practical connector layers for model-driven workflows.
+- Research gaps remain in narrowly focused database-only AI automation repos; that category still has fewer than five credible GitHub-native options in the supplied snapshot.
+
+## Why This List
+The best open source AI automation tools give teams control over deployment, source code, security posture, and integration strategy. That matters in 2026 because AI automation increasingly touches internal APIs, browser sessions, documents, support queues, CI pipelines, and production infrastructure. A GitHub-only list also makes due diligence easier: you can inspect licenses, activity, primary language, contribution health, and self-hosting options before adopting a tool.
